 "key_findings": [
  "AOD/AODSIM ak5PFJets and particleFlow PFCandidates are SPLIT and uproot-readable over plain HTTPS with no CMSSW.",
  "The jet->constituent PtrVector (obj.dau) is NOT readable \u2014 constituent-level HOJD features require re-clustering anti-kt R=0.5 from the PFCandidate collection.",
  "GenEventInfoProduct / GenJets / genParticles are UNSPLIT in AODSIM \u2014 per-event generator weight and pthat are NOT obtainable without CMSSW.",
  "run/lumi/event ARE recoverable from raw edm::EventAuxiliary bytes (BE uint32 at offsets 43/47/51 in the checked file); validated 5679/5679 events inside the golden JSON.",
  "mJetArea == 0.0 for all 108,120 jets checked in a cms-5 file \u2014 jet area is not populated in the 2010 AOD.",
  "4,378 of 6,151 files (3.879 TB) are on CTA tape: hot EOS returns HTTP 404, the cold uri times out. The MadGraph+Pythia6 leg has ONE online file per record (480 and 3,789 events) \u2014 a matched three-family test is tape-blocked there.",
  "No MOD-style derived per-jet product exists for CMS 2010 \u2014 unlike 2011A. AOD or nothing.",
  "7 TeV Herwig++ QCD exists ONLY in the Summer12-LowPU2010 production => 2010 is the only year where all three generator families coexist at 7 TeV.",
  "These 2010 records are Summer12-LowPU2010_DR42, PU_S0 (zero pileup), CMSSW 4.2.8, START42_V17B \u2014 a different year/tune/pileup era from the delivered 2011A STAGE1 table."
 ],
 "deferred": {
  "bulk_bytes": 6264892341783,
  "reason": "AOD bulk not mirrored: 6.265 TB, GitHub release cap 2 GiB, and the thread cannot materialise release binaries. Every file is directly fetchable from CERN via the https_url in the per-record index.",
  "tape_bytes": 3878959067569,
